# The sun's shadow over a forest of the modern spruce (reports/engine/2026-11-16-modern-trees/shadow-flicker.md):
# view near-30 of perf-trees.bench, the camera on the rock hill 30 m from the forest's edge, at noon, held still:
# 8 s of frame timing, a still, a 25 s clip; then a still of view inside (inside the block of 64, perf-trees view-1).
# Before the fix the hill under the camera and the valley went black in pieces of shadow pages in some frames.
# Run with a set of `scripts/content/fir_set.py forest` (--count 0 is the control):
#   OPENGOTHIC_CONTENT=<set> OPENGOTHIC_VSM_STATS=1 TEMPEST_WINDOW_SIZE=1920x1080 BENCH_HOST=ryzen \
#     scripts/bench.sh tree-shadow-flicker <out>
# OPENGOTHIC_VSM_STATS=1 logs the pairs every 5 s and waits for the GPU then: leave it out of a timing run.
# measure: python3 reports/engine/2026-11-16-modern-trees/shadow_flicker.py <out>/near-30.mp4
# @timeout 600
seed 73013
cheat god
set time 12 0
overlay off
ui off
view full
walkmode run
watch player
goto pos 48765 6250 -3156
clear 5000
cam at 48765 6679 -3156 54140 2190 -10780
# twenty real seconds after the teleport for loading, as perf-trees.bench
wait 20000
perf sample tree-shadow-flicker/near-30
wait 8000
perf stop
shot near-30
wait 200
rec near-30
wait 25000
stop
wait 500
goto pos 54140 1650 -10780
clear 3000
cam at 54140 1760 -10780 60000 2060 -10780
wait 20000
shot inside
wait 200
